# Graphify — shared knowledge artifacts are tracked; local state is not.
# Pattern follows Graphify-Labs/graphify discussion #426 (maintainer-confirmed):
# graph.json, graph.html and GRAPH_REPORT.md are the artifacts teammates and AI
# assistants query. manifest.json is mtime-based and invalid after a clone.
# Tracked here as well, because they are the durable knowledge this repo builds:
#   memory/      one file per saved exploration (question + verified answer)
#   reflections/ LESSONS.md, deterministically generated from memory/ by `reflect`
#   findings/    decisions.jsonl (the log) and decisions.md (its rendered roll-up)
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/wiki/
graphify-out/.graphify_*
# Derived exports are regenerable and no longer produced by default (see
# .agents/scripts/graphify.sh: exports are opt-in via --export). They are ignored
# anyway so that running `export` once cannot stage tens of megabytes of
# wiki/, obsidian/, svg or callflow HTML.
graphify-out/obsidian/
graphify-out/graph.svg
graphify-out/GRAPH_TREE.html
graphify-out/*-callflow.html
graphify-out/20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
graphify-out/reflections/*.bak*
graphify-out/findings/*.pre-provenance-backup

# Agent Runtime, Harness & Workspace State (per-developer, never shared)
/.agent
/.agents
/.omp
/.codex
/conductor
/AGENTS.md
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
